The memory bandwidth benchmark of benchmarks/bandwidth, on small arrays,
so that it keeps building and validating: sequentially, and on the host's
threads, where OpenMP runs its target regions when there is no device.
Each run checks the arrays' final values and prints the table only if
they are right.

RUN: merkc -O2 -fdo-loops %S/../../benchmarks/bandwidth/bandwidth.m -o %t.sequential
RUN: env BANDWIDTH_ARRAY_SIZE=100003 BANDWIDTH_NUM_TIMES=5 %t.sequential | FileCheck %s
RUN: merkc -O2 -fopenmp -fdo-loops %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/bandwidth/bandwidth.m -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_NUM_THREADS=4 BANDWIDTH_ARRAY_SIZE=100003 BANDWIDTH_NUM_TIMES=5 %t | FileCheck %s
CHECK: Running kernels 5 times
CHECK-NOT: Validation failed
CHECK: Function    MBytes/sec  Min (sec)   Max         Average
CHECK-NEXT: Copy
CHECK-NEXT: Mul
CHECK-NEXT: Add
CHECK-NEXT: Triad
CHECK-NEXT: Dot
